# Laravel Project Context and Source of Truth

## Mandatory context
- Treat `/docs/**` as the canonical product and business source of truth.
- Treat `/laravel/docs/**` as the canonical Laravel technical specification.
- Read the relevant shared and Laravel documents before implementing a feature.
- Do not silently invent business rules, financial behavior, delivery states, or permissions.
- When a requirement is explicitly marked pending, do not implement a definitive behavior unless the user approves it.

## Architecture boundary
- Laravel is the authoritative backend for authentication, authorization, delivery state, pricing, negotiation, payment, commission, refund, payout, audit, and synchronization acceptance.
- Flutter is a client, not a source of truth.
- All critical client-supplied values MUST be validated on the server.

## Core domain
- Business, Driver, Vehicle, Delivery, DeliveryItem, Offer, CounterOffer, Payment, Commission, Refund, Payout, DeliveryEvent, DriverLocation, ProofOfDelivery, SyncEvent, Notification are domain concepts documented elsewhere.
- A Driver may have multiple active deliveries.
- A delivery still has exactly one authoritative state machine even when a driver has multiple deliveries.

## Non-negotiable rules
- Preserve auditability.
- Preserve idempotency for retryable critical operations.
- Protect concurrent delivery acceptance and financial operations with transactional consistency.
- Never derive historical financial truth from current configuration.
- Do not move backend business rules into controllers, jobs, listeners, or API resources when they belong to application/domain services.
